1177:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****     /* (From Stevens TCP/IP Illustrated Vol II, p970.) Its only a
1178:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * duplicate ack if:
1179:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * 1) It doesn't ACK new data
1180:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * 2) length of received packet is zero (i.e. no payload)
1181:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * 3) the advertised window hasn't changed
1182:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * 4) There is outstanding unacknowledged data (retransmission timer running)
1183:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * 5) The ACK is == biggest ACK sequence number so far seen (snd_una)
1184:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      *
1185:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * If it passes all five, should process as a dupack:
1186:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * a) dupacks < 3: do nothing
1187:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * b) dupacks == 3: fast retransmit
1188:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * c) dupacks > 3: increase cwnd
1189:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      *
1190:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * If it only passes 1-3, should reset dupack counter (and add to
1191:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * stats, which we don't do in lwIP)
1192:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      *
1193:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      * If it only passes 1, should reset dupack counter
1194:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      *
1195:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/tcp_in.c ****      */
